---
layout: default
openGraph:
  type: article
scripts:
  - /assets/scripts/toc-scrollspy.js
  - /assets/scripts/copy-link.js
  - /assets/scripts/copy-code.js
---
<article class="wrapper post">
  <div class="post__grid">
    {%- comment -%}
      Filled in by the `toc` build transform (lib/toc.js), which moves the table of contents here
      from wherever {% include "toc.md" %} appears in the article body. Left empty (and hidden via
      CSS :empty) for posts that don't request a TOC.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <aside class="post__toc" id="post-toc"><!--eleventy-toc-slot--></aside>
    <div class="post__main">
      <header class="post__header">
        <div class="post__meta">
          <time datetime="{{ page.date | machineDate }}">{{ page.date | readableDate }}</time>
          <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span>{{ content | readingTime }} min read</span>
          {%- if lastUpdated -%}
          <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span>
          <span>Updated {{ lastUpdated | readableDate }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
        <h1 class="post__title" data-pagefind-meta="title" style="view-transition-name: view-{{ page.fileSlug }};">{{ title }}</h1>
        {%- assign postTags = tags | publicTags -%}
        {%- if postTags.size > 0 -%}
        <ul class="tag-list">
          {%- for tag in postTags -%}
          <li><a class="tag" href="/tags/{{ tag | slugify }}/">{{ tag }}</a></li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if description -%}
        <p class="post__subtitle">{{ description }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {% include "components/share.liquid" %}
      </header>
      {%- if coverImage -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Deliberately outside .post__header (which is capped at --prose-width like the rest of the
        reading column) so the cover image can fill .post__main's full width instead of matching
        in-article image sizing — see the .cover-image rules in _prose.scss for why.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {% include "postImage.html" src: coverImage, alt: title, description: imageDescription, credits: imageCredits, className: "cover-image" %}
      {%- endif -%}
      <div class="prose">
        {{ content }}
      </div>
      <footer class="post__footer">
        <a href="/blog/">&larr; Back to all posts</a>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</article>
